WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.820
If you're wondering why David is blindfolding me,

2
00:00:02.820 --> 00:00:06.000
it's because he's going to kidnap me and take me to some random city in Serbia,

3
00:00:06.280 --> 00:00:08.660
where I'll take off the blindfold and try to guess where I am.

4
00:00:08.660 --> 00:00:10.240
Doesn't that remind you of something?

5
00:00:10.600 --> 00:00:12.200
Who knows where this guy has taken me?

6
00:00:12.200 --> 00:00:13.080
How long have we been driving?

7
00:00:13.080 --> 00:00:14.260
Two and a half hours for sure?

8
00:00:14.940 --> 00:00:17.240
Today we have a Geoguessr challenge.

9
00:00:17.240 --> 00:00:20.800
David will blindfold me, put me in the car and drive me around the city,

10
00:00:20.800 --> 00:00:23.360
to test how well I know my own city.

11
00:00:23.740 --> 00:00:24.940
Honestly, I have no idea where I am.

12
00:00:25.640 --> 00:00:30.860
When they leave me somewhere, I take off the blindfold and have to point out exactly on the map where I am.

13
00:00:31.020 --> 00:00:34.880
If I guess all five places in Vlasotince — that's the city where I live —

14
00:00:34.880 --> 00:00:38.780
David will take me somewhere deep into Serbia and drop me in an unfamiliar city.

15
00:00:39.020 --> 00:00:42.200
And I'll have to find my bearings and work out where I am, without anyone's help.

16
00:00:44.680 --> 00:00:48.260
Geoguessr is a game where you have five rounds to guess five places.

17
00:00:48.860 --> 00:00:51.580
In each round they drop you somewhere on the Google map,

18
00:00:51.580 --> 00:00:55.720
and you have to figure out what place it is and click the exact point on the map.

19
00:00:55.720 --> 00:00:58.220
The closer you guess, the more points you get.

20
00:00:58.360 --> 00:01:03.080
And today, instead of sitting at the computer, we're playing Geoguessr in real life.

21
00:01:03.260 --> 00:01:08.680
In the game you can choose the whole world, some country, or mark yourself where you want to play.

22
00:01:08.840 --> 00:01:14.020
So before the real-life challenge I chose Vlasotince in the game — to see how hard it would be.

23
00:01:14.160 --> 00:01:17.220
The first place we got was some field.

24
00:01:17.560 --> 00:01:19.420
A friend of mine lives somewhere around here.

25
00:01:20.140 --> 00:01:20.520
Somewhere here.

26
00:01:21.800 --> 00:01:24.720
Five meters of difference, so five thousand points.

27
00:01:24.720 --> 00:01:28.520
If I walk all the way down, I'll come out at the "Knez" gas station.

28
00:01:28.800 --> 00:01:29.980
All the way up.

29
00:01:30.340 --> 00:01:31.460
I'm somewhere in the middle here.

30
00:01:31.600 --> 00:01:32.640
Here you go, five thousand points.

31
00:01:33.100 --> 00:01:34.640
All right, just two meters.

32
00:01:34.720 --> 00:01:38.320
Right in front of the administration building, in the center, so somewhere here.

33
00:01:40.040 --> 00:01:40.970
Zero meters.

34
00:01:41.420 --> 00:01:44.800
The fourth place is literally the entrance to the NIS Petrol gas station.

35
00:01:46.500 --> 00:01:47.680
Why did I put it there?

36
00:01:48.140 --> 00:01:51.080
And the last place is literally by the stadium.

37
00:01:51.800 --> 00:01:52.380
Yes, somewhere here.

38
00:01:56.560 --> 00:01:58.420
This won't be as easy as I thought.

39
00:01:59.220 --> 00:02:00.380
First: where's your phone?

40
00:02:00.600 --> 00:02:01.160
Here it is, in my pocket.

41
00:02:01.380 --> 00:02:02.040
Turn off the GPS.

42
00:02:02.400 --> 00:02:03.180
Oh, damn.

43
00:02:03.380 --> 00:02:04.700
There, location services.

44
00:02:06.160 --> 00:02:06.880
Oh, it's off.

45
00:02:07.000 --> 00:02:07.480
There you go.

46
00:02:09.730 --> 00:02:12.810
I'm not used to driving and not seeing where I'm going.

47
00:02:13.130 --> 00:02:17.510
If the police show up, how do I explain that I wasn't kidnapped and I'm playing a game?

48
00:02:17.790 --> 00:02:19.190
I came here with a blindfold on.

49
00:02:19.370 --> 00:02:20.290
I'm completely lost.

50
00:02:20.490 --> 00:02:23.750
Just like when you buy a car on your own, without anyone's help.

51
00:02:23.990 --> 00:02:26.410
So while I'm spinning around and can't figure out where I am,

52
00:02:26.410 --> 00:02:30.630
let me explain how carVertical opens people's eyes when they want to buy a car.

53
00:02:30.950 --> 00:02:33.570
If you've found a great car and the price is great,

54
00:02:33.570 --> 00:02:35.730
maybe it's too good to be true.

55
00:02:35.910 --> 00:02:38.410
From this spot where I am now, I'm not allowed to move,

56
00:02:38.530 --> 00:02:42.050
I can only turn around my axis and guess where I am.

57
00:02:42.970 --> 00:02:46.630
Meet that person, but instead of a mechanic, bring only your phone.

58
00:02:46.950 --> 00:02:48.510
Ugh, damn, it's so bright.

59
00:02:48.510 --> 00:02:51.590
On carVertical just enter the car's chassis number.

60
00:02:51.710 --> 00:02:54.770
You'll be surprised when you see the mileage was rolled back by 200,000 km

61
00:02:54.770 --> 00:02:58.590
or that it was wrecked in an accident and patched up like leaky pants.

62
00:02:59.090 --> 00:03:03.680
Phew, phew, phew, phew.

63
00:03:04.660 --> 00:03:10.220
carVertical works with car dealerships, service centers, customs, insurers and police all over the world.

64
00:03:10.440 --> 00:03:13.820
Every detail about every car goes into their database.

65
00:03:13.960 --> 00:03:16.500
And if everything shows green, you can buy it.

66
00:03:16.560 --> 00:03:19.760
And if you do run into some problem, you'll be able to knock the price down nicely.

67
00:03:19.760 --> 00:03:22.580
I think I'm somewhere in this half, across the river.

68
00:03:22.680 --> 00:03:28.880
And I think I'm somewhere near Nevička, or maybe even somewhere here, on this street.

69
00:03:29.000 --> 00:03:31.160
I'll probably buy a new car next year.

70
00:03:31.280 --> 00:03:33.860
But since I bought the car I drive now blind too,

71
00:03:34.020 --> 00:03:36.320
I checked it and saw that its condition isn't the best.

72
00:03:36.480 --> 00:03:38.640
And how can you be sure you've never walked down this street?

73
00:03:38.740 --> 00:03:39.420
Well, I'm sure.

74
00:03:39.640 --> 00:03:43.380
I think it's somewhere near the Rosulje district in Vlasotince, but actually I have no idea.

75
00:03:43.760 --> 00:03:48.140
Fine, let it be the intersection of Narodnih heroja and Stojana Petrovića streets.

76
00:03:48.140 --> 00:03:49.360
That's my final answer.

77
00:03:49.500 --> 00:03:50.180
Let's see where we are.

78
00:03:50.740 --> 00:03:52.340
How far off was I, about?

79
00:03:52.440 --> 00:03:53.220
150 meters.

80
00:03:53.440 --> 00:03:55.220
So I clicked here, and we're here.

81
00:03:55.560 --> 00:03:56.520
Let's see how much that is.

82
00:03:56.660 --> 00:03:58.220
150 meters of difference.

83
00:03:58.600 --> 00:04:01.120
To check three cars you need less than 2000 dinars.

84
00:04:01.220 --> 00:04:04.640
But if you enter the code NOTALEKSA, you get an extra 30% discount.

85
00:04:04.880 --> 00:04:05.800
The link is in the video description.

86
00:04:06.020 --> 00:04:06.640
So, guys.

87
00:04:06.940 --> 00:04:08.400
I found the first place.

88
00:04:08.540 --> 00:04:10.140
The difference is only 150 meters,

89
00:04:10.140 --> 00:04:14.100
so let's count that as four and a half thousand points out of 5000.

90
00:04:15.300 --> 00:04:16.600
On to the second place.

91
00:04:16.980 --> 00:04:19.420
At the first place I earned four and a half thousand points.

92
00:04:19.580 --> 00:04:21.020
And I can say I was lucky.

93
00:04:21.460 --> 00:04:24.380
But the second place will give me a bit more trouble.

94
00:04:24.840 --> 00:04:27.460
And I was so sure I knew this city like the back of my hand.

95
00:04:27.660 --> 00:04:30.940
Write in the comments if you want me to test David later.

96
00:04:31.040 --> 00:04:33.340
Let's see if David can guess where he is.

97
00:04:35.620 --> 00:04:36.260
We're here.

98
00:04:36.520 --> 00:04:37.280
We're here, right?

99
00:04:37.320 --> 00:04:37.840
We're here.

100
00:04:39.760 --> 00:04:41.460
Even now that I see it, I still don't know where we are.

101
00:04:42.220 --> 00:04:43.020
So, guys.

102
00:04:44.040 --> 00:04:45.160
Taking off the blindfold now.

103
00:04:47.980 --> 00:04:48.620
Oh, phew.

104
00:04:50.320 --> 00:04:51.200
Damn, bro.

105
00:04:55.820 --> 00:04:57.440
There isn't even a sign here.

106
00:05:00.300 --> 00:05:01.780
I have no idea where David has brought me.

107
00:05:01.860 --> 00:05:03.220
There's literally not even a sign here.

108
00:05:03.480 --> 00:05:04.800
Okay, I think I know where we are.

109
00:05:05.120 --> 00:05:06.560
Actually I had no idea.

110
00:05:06.800 --> 00:05:07.760
I think I know where we are.

111
00:05:07.760 --> 00:05:10.480
What's more, I think in the real Geoguessr I was dropped here by chance.

112
00:05:10.560 --> 00:05:13.040
I was convinced it's the same place as recently.

113
00:05:13.760 --> 00:05:15.360
I'll assume we're right here.

114
00:05:15.740 --> 00:05:16.640
That's my final answer.

115
00:05:16.780 --> 00:05:18.520
And that's my final answer.

116
00:05:18.840 --> 00:05:21.680
So, guys, how many meters did I miss by?

117
00:05:21.940 --> 00:05:22.920
Six hundred meters.

118
00:05:23.080 --> 00:05:23.560
Well, three.

119
00:05:23.900 --> 00:05:25.140
Three and a half thousand points.

120
00:05:25.360 --> 00:05:26.540
I was close, really not bad.

121
00:05:27.200 --> 00:05:28.260
Yeah, you were close.

122
00:05:28.400 --> 00:05:29.160
Console yourself, sure.

123
00:05:29.480 --> 00:05:31.560
Now David is driving me to the third place.

124
00:05:31.840 --> 00:05:33.920
No need to remind me, there, putting this on my eyes.

125
00:05:33.920 --> 00:05:35.280
I knew this one pretty well.

126
00:05:35.380 --> 00:05:35.860
No, actually I didn't.

127
00:05:35.980 --> 00:05:36.500
Really didn't.

128
00:05:36.600 --> 00:05:37.740
Hopefully I'll guess the next one.

129
00:05:37.860 --> 00:05:38.980
David, let's go.

130
00:05:39.120 --> 00:05:42.240
With 8000 points total, we're heading to the third place.

131
00:05:43.600 --> 00:05:45.540
Absolutely no clue where he's taken me now.

132
00:05:45.600 --> 00:05:47.560
We've been driving for at least 20 minutes.

133
00:05:54.460 --> 00:05:56.540
So we're not right at the spot.

134
00:05:58.040 --> 00:05:59.120
Come on, just walk straight.

135
00:06:08.860 --> 00:06:10.200
Are you sure I know this place?

136
00:06:10.380 --> 00:06:10.680
Well, you do.

137
00:06:11.780 --> 00:06:13.500
Are you sure I know this place?

138
00:06:14.880 --> 00:06:16.020
I think I hear chickens somewhere.

139
00:06:18.100 --> 00:06:18.500
Phew.

140
00:06:22.760 --> 00:06:23.160
I know.

141
00:06:23.960 --> 00:06:24.760
I know, I know.

142
00:06:24.880 --> 00:06:25.720
I know exactly where we are.

143
00:06:28.610 --> 00:06:32.050
Judging by this terrain and by this latitude and longitude,

144
00:06:32.430 --> 00:06:35.870
the only thing I can conclude is that up there is Jastrebac.

145
00:06:36.110 --> 00:06:39.770
And we're right next to the valley, as it is,

146
00:06:39.990 --> 00:06:44.610
so I assume... wait, I'm not sure now, a second, a second, I'm not quite sure.

147
00:06:44.610 --> 00:06:47.410
As far as I can see, up there is that viewing platform.

148
00:06:48.250 --> 00:06:53.630
So somewhere... Anyway, guys, my final answer — we're here.

149
00:06:53.750 --> 00:06:54.870
Was I close?

150
00:06:55.390 --> 00:06:55.810
Exactly.

151
00:06:55.930 --> 00:06:59.890
I guessed the exact place, but missed by how many meters, go on, tell me?

152
00:07:00.050 --> 00:07:00.870
By 10 meters.

153
00:07:01.050 --> 00:07:02.950
4990 points.

154
00:07:03.250 --> 00:07:06.270
I was too modest, there, I'm giving myself 5000 points.

155
00:07:10.400 --> 00:07:12.960
Okay, guys, now we're at the fourth place.

156
00:07:13.100 --> 00:07:16.920
I can't move from this spot, I have to take the blindfold off and guess where I am.

157
00:07:22.080 --> 00:07:26.340
This guy finds me literally the emptiest and most nondescript streets.

158
00:07:26.540 --> 00:07:28.000
I think I have an idea where we are.

159
00:07:28.320 --> 00:07:34.680
Look, a meadow like this and a parked van on the other side — I know there's something like that on Radnička.

160
00:07:34.860 --> 00:07:38.500
For the previous places I had at least some idea where I was.

161
00:07:38.800 --> 00:07:41.620
And here I have some faint feeling, but I'm not sure.

162
00:07:41.840 --> 00:07:43.240
This one, Sreten Dimanić street.

163
00:07:43.360 --> 00:07:45.940
Let's see if I'm at least a little close.

164
00:07:46.240 --> 00:07:47.480
Guys, what?

165
00:07:47.760 --> 00:07:48.740
Right across the road.

166
00:07:48.920 --> 00:07:49.780
220 meters.

167
00:07:49.780 --> 00:07:51.160
As Žika Pavlović says:

168
00:07:51.160 --> 00:07:52.580
My instinct never deceives me.

169
00:07:53.600 --> 00:07:54.660
Let it be 4200.

170
00:07:54.780 --> 00:07:56.660
4200 points, says David, so...

171
00:07:56.760 --> 00:07:59.000
Okay, now we'll cross the meadow — you're over there.

172
00:07:59.080 --> 00:08:00.220
Let it be 4600.

173
00:08:00.500 --> 00:08:01.040
4500.

174
00:08:01.480 --> 00:08:01.800
4500.

175
00:08:02.220 --> 00:08:02.420
Let's go.

176
00:08:02.980 --> 00:08:05.520
That brings us to 17,500 points.

177
00:08:09.020 --> 00:08:09.560
Let's go.

178
00:08:09.560 --> 00:08:22.300
By the smell of the air and the sound, I feel we're near some bigger road.

179
00:08:23.980 --> 00:08:25.040
Guys, I know where we are.

180
00:08:25.740 --> 00:08:26.620
I literally know where we are.

181
00:08:27.020 --> 00:08:29.440
I know this house here, I know that house over there behind.

182
00:08:29.700 --> 00:08:31.500
Somewhere near here lives...

183
00:08:31.500 --> 00:08:33.160
Ljubković, my friend from elementary school.

184
00:08:33.400 --> 00:08:33.920
Somewhere here.

185
00:08:36.340 --> 00:08:41.920
The last place, in quotation marks the hardest: a hit, 5000 points, zero meters off.

186
00:08:41.920 --> 00:08:46.320
In the end we have 22,500 out of 25,000 points,

187
00:08:46.320 --> 00:08:51.840
which means I put the blindfold on again and let David take me anywhere in Serbia.

188
00:09:08.810 --> 00:09:10.350
Are we in some village? Where did we arrive?

189
00:09:10.630 --> 00:09:11.130
I'm not allowed to talk.

190
00:09:12.630 --> 00:09:13.190
Okay.

191
00:09:16.570 --> 00:09:17.610
Oh, damn.

192
00:09:19.030 --> 00:09:23.150
So, in this part of the challenge I can move around, go wherever I want.

193
00:09:23.490 --> 00:09:24.350
Well, let's go.

194
00:09:28.870 --> 00:09:31.890
I think this looks like some kind of ghost town, damn, where did you bring me?

195
00:09:32.570 --> 00:09:33.970
Everything is broken.

196
00:09:35.070 --> 00:09:36.210
The houses are empty.

197
00:09:36.550 --> 00:09:38.790
I don't know what that is down there, literally everything is empty.

198
00:09:39.930 --> 00:09:41.570
Is there some sign down there?

199
00:09:41.570 --> 00:09:46.330
So far I literally have no idea what town this is, or what settlement, but there are cars here.

200
00:09:46.690 --> 00:09:47.830
And there's a yellow sign down there, guys.

201
00:09:48.050 --> 00:09:49.790
Look at what the houses look like here.

202
00:09:50.130 --> 00:09:51.890
Like I'm in some Texan movie.

203
00:09:52.190 --> 00:09:55.590
Before we get to the sign — I saw something written on this spring.

204
00:09:55.950 --> 00:09:59.030
Spring water from the Komarica source, number seven.

205
00:09:59.470 --> 00:10:00.330
Welcome.

206
00:10:01.330 --> 00:10:04.090
Komarica is the village Žika is from.

207
00:10:04.090 --> 00:10:07.070
But we drove for two hours, bro, there's no way we were driving uphill.

208
00:10:07.450 --> 00:10:07.990
How are you?

209
00:10:08.470 --> 00:10:09.330
Fine, bro.

210
00:10:10.030 --> 00:10:11.070
Ugh, damn, this water is so cold.

211
00:10:11.410 --> 00:10:15.010
Okay, let's go look at that sign down there, since we haven't figured anything out from here.

212
00:10:15.490 --> 00:10:16.690
Komarička street.

213
00:10:17.050 --> 00:10:18.090
Is this Komarica, David?

214
00:10:18.290 --> 00:10:19.430
No, now I really don't know.

215
00:10:20.090 --> 00:10:24.310
I mean, this looks like some village, but it doesn't look like...

216
00:10:24.310 --> 00:10:26.490
Literally all the houses are broken and ruined like this,

217
00:10:26.490 --> 00:10:29.370
as if I were in some abandoned town in some Texan movie.

218
00:10:29.370 --> 00:10:31.310
What on earth is this, damn?

219
00:10:32.730 --> 00:10:38.670
This first car has Pirot plates, which means we're really not far,

220
00:10:38.670 --> 00:10:41.230
but it's definitely not Pirot.

221
00:10:41.590 --> 00:10:42.210
Although how would I know?

222
00:10:42.590 --> 00:10:45.670
I'll check the map to see what suburbs Pirot even has.

223
00:10:46.630 --> 00:10:50.250
Staničenje, Gradašnica, Gnjilan, Berilovac...

224
00:10:50.250 --> 00:10:53.570
Maybe it's Gnjilan, it sounds like a place David would take me.

225
00:10:54.150 --> 00:10:54.670
Linovo.

226
00:10:55.290 --> 00:10:57.410
Guys, we found a signpost for Linovo.

227
00:10:57.590 --> 00:10:59.170
Let's see where Linovo is.

228
00:11:01.030 --> 00:11:01.750
Quiet, doggie.

229
00:11:02.730 --> 00:11:06.290
Something tells me David chose Gnjilan for some reason.

230
00:11:06.910 --> 00:11:10.630
By the way, guys, I see a sign down there, it's probably the sign at the entrance to a settlement.

231
00:11:10.830 --> 00:11:14.910
And even if I find a sign, if I see what settlement this is, I'm not allowed to search on Google Maps,

232
00:11:15.150 --> 00:11:17.790
I have to scroll the map manually and find where I am.

233
00:11:18.270 --> 00:11:19.970
By the way, look how blind I am.

234
00:11:20.510 --> 00:11:22.650
The name of the settlement is literally written up there.

235
00:11:25.740 --> 00:11:30.140
It says on this pole: ED Jugoistok, Babušnica.

236
00:11:31.040 --> 00:11:35.080
So... but this still doesn't look like Babušnica to me.

237
00:11:35.160 --> 00:11:36.720
I think Babušnica is bigger.

238
00:11:37.060 --> 00:11:39.260
It can't be Babušnica, let me check.

239
00:11:39.820 --> 00:11:42.540
So we're somewhere between Pirot and Babušnica.

240
00:11:42.960 --> 00:11:45.740
So Pirot is that way, and Leskovac is that way.

241
00:11:46.380 --> 00:11:48.580
Let me see what's written on the sign.

242
00:11:48.840 --> 00:11:52.460
By the way, my eyesight is really bad, I need to walk right up to the sign.

243
00:11:52.460 --> 00:11:54.980
Wait, something's written on this establishment, let me look.

244
00:11:58.040 --> 00:11:59.020
Guys, look what it says.

245
00:12:00.780 --> 00:12:01.220
Ljuberađa.

246
00:12:01.840 --> 00:12:04.020
So this isn't Gorčinci, it's Ljuberađa after all.

247
00:12:04.680 --> 00:12:06.420
So, now — the Ljuberađa spring.

248
00:12:06.600 --> 00:12:08.700
